KNOWNBUG: [temp.variadic]/5 + [expr.const] -- when a constexpr member function
template body forms an outer template-id with multiple arguments, one of which
is a template-id containing a pack expansion (`And<bc<true>, And<ge<Ts,
Us>...>>::value`), CBMC does not expand the nested pack (it is not at the top of
the outer argument), so the constexpr call cannot be folded and the assertion is
dropped (vacuous).  This is the remaining blocker for std::get on a std::tuple:
libstdc++'s _TupleConstraints::__is_explicitly_constructible nests
pack-expanding template-ids inside a multi-argument __and_.  A single zipped
expansion already folds (cpp11_constexpr_zipped_pack_expansion); reclassify CORE
once nested pack expansions in multi-argument template-ids are expanded too.
